Thanks for the hint, setting LC_NUMERIC to C works!

But I still think that this is some kind of bug: With German locale, JGR
just isn't usable. Since the comma has a completely different meaning in
R, you can't use it as decimal point:

[German locale]
> 2,3
Fehler: Syntaxfehler in Zeile "2,"

And R itself uses the dot as decimal point on the same system. It's only
within JGR when running with Java6 that it doesn't.

Maybe it would be good to add "export LC_NUMERIC=C" or something to the
run-script, as it shouldn't break anything, but help prevent this
problem.

Cheers,
Frederik

